From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adeeb Shihadeh <adeeb@comma.ai>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 04:50:55 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: trivial-devices: add the comma.ai panda

The panda is comma's CAN interface microcontroller. On the comma four it
sits on an SPI bus of the SoC and is driven from userspace through
spidev, so it needs nothing beyond a compatible, reg and
spi-max-frequency.

This is local to AGNOS, like the spidev patch that uses it.

Signed-off-by: Adeeb Shihadeh <adeeb@comma.ai>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/trivial-devices.yaml | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/trivial-devices.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/trivial-devices.yaml
index 2de8eb09cb..539d364b59 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/trivial-devices.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/trivial-devices.yaml
@@ -85,6 +85,8 @@ properties:
           - capella,cm3323
             # Cisco SPI Petra
           - cisco,spi-petra
+            # comma.ai panda CAN interface, driven from userspace through spidev
+          - commaai,panda
             # High-Precision Digital Thermometer
           - dallas,ds1631
             # Total-Elapsed-Time Recorder with Alarm
